const HELP: String = "toyanalyze [--ready] check MANIFEST JOBS [CACHE]\ntoyanalyze [--ready] session MANIFEST JOBS SESSION [CACHE]\nInput paths are relative to input; optional cache is relative to output.\nExit 0 clean, 1 toy diagnostics, 2 refusal/I/O, 3 stdout unavailable.\n"

// Read at most cap+1, preserving source size refusal under changing host files.
fn read(d: Dir, name: String, cap: u64) -> Result[unique Bytes, u64] {
  let Ok(size) = file.size(d, path.of(name)) else {
    return Error(1)
  }
  if size > cap {
    return Error(2)
  }
  let mut Ok(handle) = file.open(d, path.of(name)) else {
    return Error(1)
  }
  let mut data: List[u8] = []
  while true {
    let remaining = cap - list.len(data)
    let count = if remaining < 1024 {
      remaining + 1
    } else {
      1024u64
    }
    let Ok(n) = file.read(d, mut handle, mut data, count) else {
      return Error(1)
    }
    if n > remaining {
      return Error(2)
    }
    if n == 0 {
      break
    }
  }
  Ok(unique bytes.from_list(take data))
}

fn json_data(take data: Bytes) -> Result[json.Value, String] uses {} {
  let Ok(text) = string.from_bytes(take data) else {
    return Error("json")
  }
  let Ok(value) = json.parse(take text) else {
    return Error("json")
  }
  Ok(take value)
}

fn field(value: json.Value, key: String) -> Result[String, String] uses {} {
  let Some(Text(text)) = json_access.member(value, key) else {
    return Error("shape")
  }
  Ok(unique text)
}

fn safe_path(name: String) -> bool uses {} {
  let data = string.as_bytes(name)
  if bytes.len(data) == 0 || bytes.len(data) > 128 {
    return false
  }
  // A deliberately small portable relative-path alphabet, no traversal aliases.
  if data[0] == 47u8 || string.contains(name, "..") {
    return false
  }
  for c in data {
    if !ascii.is_alnum(c) && c != 95u8 && c != 45u8 && c != 46u8 && c != 47u8 {
      return false
    }
  }
  true
}

fn decode_manifest(value: json.Value) -> Result[List[incremental.Decl], String] uses {} {
  let Some(items_value) = json_access.member(value, "modules") else {
    return Error("shape")
  }
  let Some(items) = json_access.as_array(items_value) else {
    return Error("shape")
  }
  if list.len(items) > 16 {
    return Error("modules")
  }
  let mut declarations: List[incremental.Decl] = []
  for item in items {
    let name = field(item, "name")?
    let path = field(item, "path")?
    if !syntax.identifier(name) || !safe_path(path) {
      return Error("declaration")
    }
    for earlier in declarations {
      if earlier.name == name || earlier.path == path {
        return Error("duplicate_module")
      }
    }
    list.push(mut declarations, incremental.Decl(name: take name, path: take path))
  }
  Ok(take declarations)
}

fn file_error(code: u64) -> String uses {} {
  if code == 2 {
    "input_bytes"
  } else {
    "file"
  }
}

fn syntax_error(error: syntax.Refusal) -> String uses {} {
  match error {
    Limit(code) => unique code,
  }
}

fn syntax_code(error: syntax.Refusal) -> u64 uses {} {
  match error {
    Limit(code) => if code == "bindings" {
      3u64
    } else {
      4u64
    },
  }
}

fn worker_error(code: u64) -> String uses {} {
  if code == 3 {
    "bindings"
  } else if code == 4 {
    "ast_depth"
  } else {
    file_error(code)
  }
}

fn load(
  tasks: Tasks,
  d: Dir,
  take declarations: List[incremental.Decl],
  jobs: u64,
  ready: Option[(Dir, Path)]
) -> Result[incremental.State, String] {
  let inputs = shared.freeze(unique declarations)
  let mut state = incremental.State(modules: [])
  let mut start = 0u64
  while start < list.len(declarations) {
    let first = start
    let end = if start + jobs < list.len(declarations) {
      start + jobs
    } else {
      list.len(declarations)
    }
    let loaded = task.scope(
      tasks,
      fn(s: Scope) -> Result[List[Shared[incremental.Module]], u64] {
        let mut set: TaskSet[Result[Shared[incremental.Module], u64]] of s = task.set(s)
        for slot in first..end {
          let index = slot
          task.add(
            s,
            mut set,
            task.async(
              s,
              fn() -> Result[Shared[incremental.Module], u64] {
                shared.with(
                  inputs,
                  fn(items: List[incremental.Decl]) -> Result[
                    Shared[incremental.Module],
                    u64
                  ] {
                    let data = read(d, items[index].path, syntax.SOURCE_BYTES)?
                    let item = incremental.make(unique items[index], data) ? syntax_code
                    Ok(shared.freeze(unique item))
                  }
                )
              }
            )
          )
        }
        if first == 0 {
          if let Some((ready_dir, ready_path)) = ready {
            let admitted = shared.with(
              inputs,
              fn(items: List[incremental.Decl]) -> Result[(), u64] {
                for index in first..end {
                  let Ok(info) = file.metadata(d, path.of(items[index].path)) else {
                    return Error(1)
                  }
                  if info.kind != Regular() {
                    return Error(1)
                  }
                  let Ok(size) = file.size(d, path.of(items[index].path)) else {
                    return Error(1)
                  }
                  if size > syntax.SOURCE_BYTES {
                    return Error(2)
                  }
                }
                Ok(())
              }
            )
            if let Error(code) = admitted {
              task.cancel_all(s, take set)
              return Error(code)
            }
            if let Error(_) = file.write_bytes(ready_dir, ready_path, b"ready") {
              task.cancel_all(s, take set)
              return Error(1)
            }
          }
        }
        task.all(s, take set)
      }
    ) ? worker_error
    for slot in 0u64..list.len(loaded) {
      let item = shared.with(
        loaded[slot],
        fn(value: incremental.Module) -> incremental.Module {
          unique value
        }
      )
      list.push(mut state.modules, take item)
    }
    start = end
  }
  Ok(take state)
}

fn print_check(output: Stdout, tasks: Tasks, mut state: incremental.State, jobs: u64) -> Result[
  u8,
  String
] {
  let checked = incremental.check(tasks, mut state, jobs)
  let text = report.check(checked, state)
  let Ok(()) = out.print(output, f"{text}\n") else {
    return Error("output")
  }
  Ok(
    if checked.total == 0 {
      0u8
    } else {
      1u8
    }
  )
}

fn validate_commands(state: incremental.State, commands: List[json.Value]) -> Result[
  (),
  String
] uses {} {
  let mut edits = 0u64
  // Validate the entire session before applying its first replacement.
  for command in commands {
    if let Some(replacement) = json_access.member(command, "replace") {
      edits += 1
      if edits > 32 {
        return Error("edits")
      }
      let name = field(replacement, "module")?
      let source = field(replacement, "source")?
      if incremental.find(state, name) == None() {
        return Error("edit_module")
      }
      if string.byte_len(source) > syntax.SOURCE_BYTES {
        return Error("source_bytes")
      }
    } else if json_access.member(command, "check") != Some(Bool(true)) {
      return Error("command")
    }
  }
  Ok(())
}

fn session(
  output: Stdout,
  tasks: Tasks,
  mut state: incremental.State,
  jobs: u64,
  value: json.Value,
  mut exit: u8
) -> Result[(), String] {
  let Some(commands_value) = json_access.member(value, "commands") else {
    return Error("shape")
  }
  let Some(commands) = json_access.as_array(commands_value) else {
    return Error("shape")
  }
  if list.len(commands) > 65 {
    return Error("commands")
  }
  validate_commands(state, commands)?
  for command in commands {
    if let Some(replacement) = json_access.member(command, "replace") {
      let name = field(replacement, "module")?
      let source = field(replacement, "source")?
      let Some(index) = incremental.find(state, name) else {
        return Error("edit_module")
      }
      match incremental.replace_source(mut state, index, string.as_bytes(source)) {
        Ok(()) => {},
        Error(problem) => {
          return Error(syntax_error(problem))
        },
      }
    } else {
      exit = print_check(output, tasks, mut state, jobs)?
    }
  }
  Ok(())
}

fn execute(rt: Io, args: Args, output: Stdout) -> Result[u8, String] {
  let mut base = 0u64
  if arg.text(args, 0) == Ok("--ready") {
    let Ok(input) = io.stdin(rt) else {
      return Error("stdin")
    }
    let Ok(()) = out.print(output, "ready\n") else {
      return Error("output")
    }
    let mut bytes: List[u8] = []
    let Ok(1u64) = stdin.read(input, mut bytes, 1) else {
      return Error("stdin")
    }
    base = 1
  }
  let Ok(mode) = arg.text(args, base) else {
    return Error("usage")
  }
  let width = if mode == "session" {
    4u64
  } else if mode == "check" {
    3u64
  } else {
    return Error("usage")
  }
  let count = arg.len(args) - base
  if count < width || count > width + 1 {
    return Error("usage")
  }
  let Ok(manifest) = arg.text(args, base + 1) else {
    return Error("usage")
  }
  let Ok(jobs_text) = arg.text(args, base + 2) else {
    return Error("usage")
  }
  let jobs = if jobs_text == "1" {
    1u64
  } else if jobs_text == "2" {
    2u64
  } else if jobs_text == "3" {
    3u64
  } else if jobs_text == "4" {
    4u64
  } else {
    return Error("jobs")
  }
  if !safe_path(manifest) {
    return Error("path")
  }
  let Ok(d) = io.dir(rt, path.of("input")) else {
    return Error("file")
  }
  let Ok(tasks) = io.tasks(rt) else {
    return Error("tasks")
  }
  let manifest_value = json_data(read(d, manifest, 8192) ? file_error)?
  let declared = decode_manifest(manifest_value)?
  let mut ready: Option[(Dir, Path)] = None()
  if let Some(value) = json_access.member(manifest_value, "ready") {
    let Text(name) = value else {
      return Error("shape")
    }
    if !safe_path(name) {
      return Error("path")
    }
    let Ok(ready_dir) = io.dir(rt, path.of("output")) else {
      return Error("file")
    }
    ready = Some((ready_dir, path.of(name)))
  }
  let mut state = load(tasks, d, take declared, jobs, ready)?
  let mut exit = print_check(output, tasks, mut state, jobs)?
  if mode == "session" {
    let Ok(name) = arg.text(args, base + 3) else {
      return Error("usage")
    }
    if !safe_path(name) {
      return Error("path")
    }
    let value = json_data(read(d, name, 300000) ? file_error)?
    session(output, tasks, mut state, jobs, value, mut exit)?
  }
  if count == width + 1 {
    let Ok(name) = arg.text(args, base + width) else {
      return Error("usage")
    }
    if !safe_path(name) {
      return Error("path")
    }
    let Ok(cache_dir) = io.dir(rt, path.of("output")) else {
      return Error("cache")
    }
    match read(cache_dir, name, 300000) {
      Ok(data) => {
        if !report.validate_cache(json_data(take data)?) {
          return Error("cache")
        }
      },
      Error(_) => {
        // Only absence permits a new cache, never a denied or oversized read.
        if file.size(cache_dir, path.of(name)) != Error(NotFound()) {
          return Error("cache")
        }
      },
    }
    let text = report.cache(state)
    let mut Ok(file) = file.create_atomic(cache_dir, path.of(name)) else {
      return Error("cache")
    }
    let Ok(()) = file.write_all(cache_dir, mut file, string.as_bytes(text)) else {
      return Error("cache")
    }
    let Ok(()) = file.commit(cache_dir, take file) else {
      return Error("cache")
    }
  }
  Ok(exit)
}

pub fn main(rt: Io, args: Args) -> process.ExitCode {
  let Ok(output) = io.stdout(rt) else {
    return process.exit_code(3u8)
  }
  if arg.text(args, 0) == Ok("--help") {
    let _ = out.print(output, HELP)
    return process.SUCCESS
  }
  match execute(rt, args, output) {
    Ok(code) => process.exit_code(code),
    Error(code) => {
      let text = report.error(code)
      let _ = out.print(output, f"{text}\n")
      process.exit_code(2u8)
    },
  }
}
